eal-time financial data."], ["1982", "Merrill Lynch installs the first 22 Bloomberg terminals and takes a 30% stake in the company."], ["1986", "The company rebrands as Bloomberg L.P., consolidating its market-data and analytics identity."], ["1990", "Bloomberg Business News is launched, expanding the firm's media footprint."], ["1993", "Bloomberg reaches 25,000 terminal installations, signalling mass market acceptance."], ["1996", "Michael Bloomberg buys back 10% of the company from Merrill Lynch, increasing founder control."], ["2001", "Michael Bloomberg is elected Mayor of New York City and Peter Grauer becomes Chairman."], ["2009", "Bloomberg acquires BusinessWeek magazine to deepen its business journalism capabilities."], ["2014", "Michael Bloomberg returns to full-time leadership, steering strategic tech and data initiatives."], ["2018", "Bloomberg opens a sustainable European headquarters in London as an architectural and ESG statement."], ["2023", "Bloomberg announces BloombergGPT, a finance-focused large language model for data analysis."], ["2025", "Terminal subscriptions surpass 370,000 globally and revenue hits a record $13.2 billion."], ["2026", "Expansion into Southeast Asia and Africa becomes a primary focus to capture emerging-market demand."]]], "code_blocks": [], "meta_description": "Explore the legacy of Bloomberg's founders. Learn how their vision and leadership continue to shape the company's success today.", "meta_keywords": "What is the Brief History of Bloomberg Company?, Brief History, Business Model Canvas Research, businessmodelcanvastemplate.com", "og_image": "http://businessmodelcanvastemplate.com/cdn/shop/articles/download_b79c064f-a7d3-40f7-b425-a76e9f2e3ad4.png?v=1751056326", "js_rendered": true, "js_message": "Page appears to be rendered by a JavaScript framework; content may be incomplete.", "success": true, "error": "", "truncated": false, "fetched_bytes": 322640, "total_bytes": 322640}}